Subject: register bundles: take the record path (D13)

What this does:
  Computes `regvm_all_threaded` from the encoded bytes with a shared helper,
  `regvm_code_all_threaded`, used by the compiler and by the bundle read path
  (both the eager read and lazy materialization), and materializes a lazy
  callee before the record-eligibility test in the four call classifiers
  (`regvm_t_call`, `regvm_t_call_method`, `regvm_t_tail_call`,
  `regvm_t_tail_call_method`).

Why we need it:
  `regvm_all_threaded` is a property of the interpreter build, not of the
  bytecode, so it is never serialized. A function read from a bundle therefore
  had `regvm_call_ready == 0` and every call to it took the C path: box2d run
  from an eager bundle executed ~10% more instructions than the same source
  run directly. Recomputing it on read makes bundled code meet the record call
  and tail-call fast paths for the first time. Materializing the lazy callee
  before the eligibility test is what makes a lazy bundle's Error.stack match
  the source and eager bundle (bundle plan 4.3 case 2): otherwise the first
  call is classified ineligible and its frame survives.

Needs a bytecode version bump:
  No. The wire format is unchanged; this recomputes interpreter state on read.

Notes:
  box2d, register build, `.local/regvm-bundle/run.c`, `perf stat -e
  instructions:u`, run-only (total minus a NOEVAL load):
    source                    2,639,982,044
    eager bundle, before D13  2,901,198,420  (+10.07% vs source)
    eager bundle, after D13   2,650,720,853  (+0.41% vs source)
    lazy bundle, after D13    2,641,301,782  (+0.05% vs source)
  Gate is within 1%; box2d checksum 546.1008391043414.
  Gates: `.local/redesign/drc/run-gates.sh p0tree p0 full` with
  DRC_BASE_ERR=50 -> 8 pass / 0 fail (test262 50/81192, diff-suite 400/0/0
  mono and threaded, box2d, leak, RSS). 13-row Octane round trip: source,
  eager and lazy bundles produce identical output (scores aside). ASan build
  of run.c over all 13 rows, eager and lazy: no memory errors.

